# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 104-110 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 12 — CHAPTER 14, 2026-09-21; the one run, THE SECOND HALF): the carcass, the sojourner and
# the kid (104), the tithe's liability (105), the eating at the place (106), the way, the money and the desire (107), the Levite (108), the third year (109), the
# four at the gate (110) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files (the whole-row rule); every quotation CUT by consonants (ch14_ink.SP_ — a miss lands in FAIL,
# asserted empty by the ledger writer); a middah named only where the row argues by one (logic/MIDDOT.md, checked before typed: I1 the a fortiori, I2 the
# analogy, I3 the paradigm; the shelf's own "the verse compares" (the juxtaposition) named without a code). Speed ruling (c): CONTEXT rows terse. Chapter 13's form.
from ch14_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(104, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT EAT ANY CARCASS" (14:21) — I HAVE ONLY A CARCASS; THE TORN WHENCE? "CARCASS" — "ANY CARCASS". The head row of piska 104 ({SP_(104, 1, "טרפה", "מנין")} "the torn whence"; {SP_(104, 1, "כל", "נבלה")} "any carcass"): THE TORN READ INTO "ANY" — Leviticus 17:15\'s and 22:8\'s "carcass or torn" (by CALL; 14:21 shares no clause with them, asserted) supplied here from the particle; the exam: Chullin 72b-73a. Fresh.')
srow(104, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO THE SOJOURNER WITHIN YOUR GATES" — IT TEACHES THAT ONE GIVES IT AS A GIFT TO A RESIDENT ALIEN. ({SP_(104, 2, "שנותנה", "במתנה", "לגר", "תושב")} "that one gives it as a gift to a resident alien"): THE SOJOURNER OF THE GATES THE RESIDENT ALIEN — Onkelos\'s "uncircumcised sojourner" the same reading (asserted); THE INK: "to the sojourner within your gates" ONE seat. Fresh.')
srow(104, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'WHENCE EVEN TO A FOREIGNER? "TO A FOREIGNER." ({SP_(104, 3, "מנין", "אף", "לנכרי")} "whence even to a foreigner"): the gift to the foreigner too. Fresh.')
srow(104, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'WHENCE THAT ONE SELLS IT TO A RESIDENT ALIEN? "OR SELL." ({SP_(104, 4, "שמוכרה", "לגר", "תושב")} "that one sells it to a resident alien"): the sale to the alien. Fresh.')
srow(104, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE EVEN TO A FOREIGNER? "TO A FOREIGNER." WHEN YOU COME TO SAY IT: ONE SELLS IT AND GIVES IT AS A GIFT TO A FOREIGNER AND TO A RESIDENT ALIEN. ({SP_(104, 5, "מוכרה", "ונותנה", "במתנה", "לנכרי", "ולגר", "תושב")} "one sells it and gives it to a foreigner and to a resident alien"): THE TWO VERBS CROSSED OVER THE TWO PERSONS — a four-cell table from the verse\'s pairing (give to the sojourner, sell to the foreigner), each verb read to each person; the exam: Mishnah Avodah Zarah 2:6?, Pesachim 21b (R. Meir and R. Judah on the verse\'s pairing). Fresh.')
srow(104, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH SAYS: THE WORDS AS THEY ARE WRITTEN. The row without a citation ({SP_(104, 6, "דברים", "ככתבם")} "the words as they are written"): THE DISSENT — the gift to the sojourner and the sale to the foreigner as paired, no crossing (Pesachim 21b\'s dispute the exam\'s row; THE TWO ARMS A PARAMETER at the compile). Fresh.')
srow(104, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR YOU ARE A HOLY PEOPLE TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" — SANCTIFY YOURSELF: THINGS PERMITTED WHICH OTHERS TREAT AS FORBIDDEN, YOU MAY NOT TREAT AS PERMITTED BEFORE THEM. ({SP_(104, 7, "דברים", "המותרים", "ואחרים", "נהגו", "בהם", "אסור")} "things permitted which others treat as forbidden"): 97:1\'s "sanctify yourself" said again at the clause\'s second seat with A NEW LAW — the custom\'s bar (the exam: Pesachim 50b-51a); THE INK: "a holy people" twice in the chapter (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(104, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT BOIL A KID IN ITS MOTHER\'S MILK" — WHY SAID? AGAINST THE THREE COVENANTS THE HOLY ONE MADE WITH ISRAEL THREE TIMES: ONE AT HOREB, ONE IN THE PLAINS OF MOAB, ONE AT MOUNT GERIZIM AND MOUNT EBAL. ({SP_(104, 8, "כנגד", "שלש", "בריתות")} "against three covenants"; {SP_(104, 8, "אחת", "בחורב")} "one at Horeb"): THE THREE SEATS OF THE VERSE (asserted: Exodus 23:19, 34:26 identical, and this) READ AS THE THREE COVENANTS — the English\'s note: an interpolation from the Mekhilta; the row READ BEFORE at chapter 6\'s sitting (the covenants). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 6\'s sitting).')
srow(104, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA SAYS: THE WILD BEAST AND THE FOWL ARE NOT FROM THE TORAH, FOR IT SAYS "YOU SHALL NOT BOIL A KID IN ITS MOTHER\'S MILK" THREE TIMES — TO EXCLUDE THE WILD BEAST, THE FOWL AND THE UNCLEAN BEAST. ({SP_(104, 9, "חיה", "ועוף", "אינם", "מן", "התורה")} "the wild beast and the fowl are not from the Torah"; {SP_(104, 9, "פרט", "לחיה", "ועוף", "ובהמה", "טמאה")} "to exclude the wild beast, the fowl and the unclean beast"): THE THREE SEATS AS THREE EXCLUSIONS — the law\'s scope a parameter with the kid\'s kind its edge (the exam: Mishnah Chullin 8:4 the row\'s citation; Chullin 113a); the English\'s bracket the opposite sense — the Hebrew\'s "to exclude" stands. Fresh.')
srow(104, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE THE GALILEAN SAYS: IT SAYS "YOU SHALL NOT EAT ANY CARCASS" AND IT SAYS "YOU SHALL NOT BOIL A KID IN ITS MOTHER\'S MILK" — [WHAT IS FORBIDDEN AS CARCASS IS FORBIDDEN TO BOIL IN MILK; THE FOWL, FORBIDDEN AS CARCASS, MIGHT BE FORBIDDEN TO BOIL IN MILK? "IN ITS MOTHER\'S MILK" —] THE FOWL, WHICH HAS NO MOTHER\'S MILK, IS EXCLUDED. ({SP_(104, 10, "יצא", "עוף", "שאין", "לו", "חלב", "אם")} "the fowl, which has no mother\'s milk, is excluded"): THE VERSE\'S TWO CLAUSES READ TOGETHER — the carcass\'s class the milk law\'s class, the fowl out by "its mother\'s milk" (the bracketed text the editor\'s from Mishnah Chullin 8:4); the two arms (R. Akiva\'s, R. Yose\'s) the exam\'s dispute. Fresh.')
srow(105, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE ALL THE YIELD OF YOUR SEED THAT COMES FORTH FROM THE FIELD YEAR BY YEAR" (14:22) — IT TEACHES THAT ONE DOES NOT TITHE FROM ONE YEAR FOR ITS FELLOW. The head row of piska 105 ({SP_(105, 1, "שאין", "מעשרים", "אותו", "משנה", "לחברתה")} "that one does not tithe it from one year for its fellow"): "YEAR BY YEAR" READ AS EACH YEAR ITS OWN — THE INK: "year by year" ONE seat (asserted); the exam: Rosh Hashanah 12b, Bekhorot 53b. Fresh.')
srow(105, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY THE SECOND TITHE, OF WHICH SCRIPTURE SPEAKS; WHENCE TO INCLUDE THE OTHER TITHES? "TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE." The row without a citation ({SP_(105, 2, "אין", "לי", "אלא", "מעשר", "שני")} "I have only the second tithe"): THE CHAPTER\'S TITHE NAMED THE SECOND — the shelf\'s own identification of which tithe 14:22-27 is (Numbers 18\'s the first, by CALL); the doubled verb widening to all. Fresh.')
srow(105, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE OF THE CATTLE TITHE THAT ONE DOES NOT TITHE IT FROM ONE YEAR FOR ITS FELLOW? "TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE ALL THE YIELD OF YOUR SEED THAT COMES FORTH FROM THE FIELD YEAR BY YEAR." ({SP_(105, 3, "למעשר", "בהמה")} "of the cattle tithe"): the cattle tithe (Leviticus 27:32 by CALL) drawn under "year by year" — the English\'s notes name the first tithe and the pauper\'s tithe as the "other tithes" (the English cites 14:28-29). Fresh.')
srow(105, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'R. SHIMON SON OF JUDAH IN THE NAME OF R. SHIMON: WHENCE THAT THE CATTLE TITHE IS UNDER "STAND AND TITHE"? "TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE." ({SP_(105, 4, "בעמוד", "ועשר")} "stand and tithe"): the doubling read as an urging (the English\'s note: 63:3 and the Sifra on the cattle tithe). Fresh.')
srow(105, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT WHATEVER GROWS FROM THE EARTH, SUCH AS WOAD AND MADDER, BE LIABLE TO THE TITHE? "TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE … AND YOU SHALL EAT." ({SP_(105, 5, "כגון", "סטיס", "וקוצה")} "such as woad and madder"): THE EDIBLE THE CLASS — 14:23\'s "and you shall eat" the limit on 14:22\'s "all the yield" (Mishnah Maasrot 1:1 the English\'s note — the answer sheet\'s first row). Fresh.')
srow(105, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT EVEN HONEY AND MILK? "THAT COMES FORTH FROM THE FIELD YEAR BY YEAR" — SAY NOW: WHAT COMES FORTH FROM THE FIELD\'S DOMAIN. ({SP_(105, 6, "אף", "דבש", "וחלב")} "even honey and milk"; {SP_(105, 6, "היוצא", "מרשות", "שדה")} "what comes forth from the field\'s domain"): THE PARTICIPLE\'S CLAUSE THE SECOND LIMIT — the field\'s produce, not the animal\'s; THE INK: "that comes forth from the field" ONE seat, the one article-participle of the chapter (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(105, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'SINCE IT IS SAID "AND YOU SHALL EAT BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD … THE TITHE OF YOUR GRAIN, YOUR WINE AND YOUR OIL" (14:23), MIGHT ONLY GRAIN, WINE AND OIL BE LIABLE? WHENCE TO INCLUDE OTHER FRUITS? "THE YIELD OF YOUR SEED." ({SP_(105, 7, "מנין", "לרבות", "שאר", "פרות")} "whence to include other fruits"): THE TWO VERSES\' TWO LISTS — 14:23\'s three (12:17\'s list, asserted) against 14:22\'s "all" — the wider read as the law, the narrower as the rite\'s example. Fresh.')
srow(105, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'IT WOULD SAY THIS: WERE IT SO, I WOULD SAY — AS GRAIN IS DISTINCTIVE, BROUGHT IN FOR STORAGE AND EATEN AS IT IS, SO I INCLUDE ONLY ITS LIKE: RICE, MILLET, POPPY AND SESAME. WHENCE TO INCLUDE THE OTHER PULSES? "TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE." ({SP_(105, 8, "את", "האורז", "ואת", "הדוחן")} "the rice and the millet"): I3 (checked) OFFERED AND OVERRIDDEN by the doubled verb — the paradigm from grain would take four species, the doubling takes all pulse. Fresh.')
srow(105, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'I INCLUDE THE PULSES EATEN AS THEY ARE, BUT NOT YET THE LUPINE AND THE MUSTARD, NOT EATEN AS THEY ARE? "TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE." MIGHT IT BE EVEN THOUGH THEY HAVE NOT TAKEN ROOT? "AND YOU SHALL EAT." ({SP_(105, 9, "את", "התורמוס", "ואת", "החרדל")} "the lupine and the mustard"; {SP_(105, 9, "שלא", "השרישו")} "they have not taken root"): the class widened again, then the onset set by "eat" (the English\'s notes: Mishnah Maasrot 4:6, 1:3 — a third of the growth). Fresh.')
srow(105, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE TO INCLUDE VEGETABLES FOR THE TITHES? "AND ALL THE TITHE OF THE LAND" (LEVITICUS 27:30). ({SP_(105, 10, "לרבות", "ירקות", "למעשרות")} "to include vegetables for the tithes"): THE KIN VERSE BY CALL (Leviticus 27:30 read at its sitting) — the vegetables from "all" there, not from here (the English\'s note: the Sifra\'s row). Fresh.')
srow(105, 11, 'CONTEXT', f'"OF THE SEED OF THE LAND" (LEVITICUS 27:30) — TO INCLUDE GARLIC, CRESS AND ROCKET; MIGHT I INCLUDE TURNIP, RADISH AND GARDEN SEEDS NOT EATEN? "OF THE SEED OF THE LAND" — AND NOT ALL THE SEED OF THE LAND. ({SP_(105, 11, "לרבות", "שום", "שחלים", "וגרגיר")} "to include garlic, cress and rocket"): the partitive "of" the limit (Mishnah Maasrot 4:5 the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(105, 12, 'CONTEXT', f'"OF THE FRUIT OF THE TREE" (LEVITICUS 27:30) — TO INCLUDE THE FRUITS OF THE TREE. ({SP_(105, 12, "לרבות", "פרות", "האילן")} "to include the fruits of the tree"). Fresh.')
srow(105, 13, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT I INCLUDE THE SYCAMORE PODS, THE PODS OF ZALMONAH AND OF GEDERAH, NOT EATEN? "OF THE FRUIT OF THE TREE" — AND NOT ALL THE FRUIT OF THE TREE. ({SP_(105, 13, "חרובי", "שקמה")} "the sycamore pods"): the partitive again (the English\'s note on the tree\'s two words). Fresh.')
srow(105, 14, 'CONTEXT', f'WHENCE THAT A MAN TITHES WHAT HE EATS? "TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE." ({SP_(105, 14, "שאדם", "מעשר", "את", "שאוכל")} "that a man tithes what he eats"): the eater\'s own liability. Fresh.')
srow(105, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE EVEN THOUGH ITS WORK IS NOT FINISHED IN THE FIELD? "AS THE GRAIN FROM THE THRESHING-FLOOR" (NUMBERS 18:27) — AND IT IS STILL IN THE FIELD; "AND AS THE FULLNESS OF THE WINEPRESS" — UNTIL IT IS IN THE PRESS. ({SP_(105, 15, "שלא", "נגמרה", "מלאכתו", "בשדה")} "that its work is not finished in the field"): THE ONSET OF LIABILITY FROM THE LEVITES\' VERSE BY CALL (Numbers 18:27 read at its sitting) — the threshing-floor and the press the two clocks. Fresh.')
srow(105, 16, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT A MAN EAT CASUALLY IN THE FIELD? "TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE." ({SP_(105, 16, "אוכל", "ערי", "בשדה")} "eat casually in the field"): the casual eating\'s liability (the English\'s note: Mishnah Maasrot 2:4 the other way). Fresh.')
srow(105, 17, 'CONTEXT', f'WHENCE THE ONE WHO SOWS? "THAT COMES FORTH FROM THE FIELD." ({SP_(105, 17, "מנין", "שזורע")} "whence the one who sows"). Fresh.')
srow(105, 18, 'CONTEXT', f'WHENCE THE ONE WHO STORES? "THE YIELD OF YOUR SEED." ({SP_(105, 18, "מנין", "שכונס")} "whence the one who stores"): the two clauses two acts. Fresh.')
srow(105, 19, 'MATERIAL', f'THEY SAID: THE SHOPS OF THE SONS OF HANAN WERE DESTROYED THREE YEARS BEFORE THE LAND OF ISRAEL, FOR THEY TOOK THEIR FRUITS OUT OF THE TITHES, EXPOUNDING "TITHE, YOU SHALL TITHE … AND YOU SHALL EAT" — AND NOT THE SELLER; "THE YIELD OF YOUR SEED" — AND NOT THE BUYER. ({SP_(105, 19, "חרבו", "חניות", "בני", "חנן")} "the shops of the sons of Hanan were destroyed"; {SP_(105, 19, "ולא", "מוכר")} "and not the seller"): THE EVASION BY THE VERSE\'S OWN WORDS AND ITS PUNISHMENT — a run outside the Torah (the English\'s note: the Jerusalem Talmud Peah 1:6); the exam: Bava Metzia 88a. Fresh.')
srow(106, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL EAT BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD IN THE PLACE WHICH HE SHALL CHOOSE" (14:23) — R. YOSE SAYS THREE THINGS IN THE NAME OF THREE ELDERS. The head row of piska 106 ({SP_(106, 1, "שלשה", "דברים", "משום", "שלשה", "זקנים")} "three things in the name of three elders"): the frame of 106:2-4 — THE PLACE CLAUSE READ BY THREE (R. Akiva, Ben Zoma, R. Ishmael), each by the firstling\'s juxtaposition. Fresh.')
srow(106, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA: MIGHT A MAN BRING UP FIRSTLINGS FROM OUTSIDE THE LAND TO THE LAND? "AND YOU SHALL EAT BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD IN THE PLACE WHICH HE SHALL CHOOSE" — FROM THE PLACE YOU BRING THE TITHE OF GRAIN YOU BRING FIRSTLINGS; FROM OUTSIDE THE LAND, WHENCE YOU BRING NO TITHE OF GRAIN, YOU BRING NO FIRSTLINGS. ({SP_(106, 2, "ממקום", "שאתה", "מביא", "מעשר", "דגן", "אתה", "מביא", "בכורות")} "from the place you bring the tithe of grain you bring firstlings"): THE FIRSTLING AND THE TITHE ONE VERSE — the place of the one the place of the other (the English\'s note: Tosefta Sanhedrin 3:5); the firstling\'s law (15:19-23) NEVER READ AHEAD, its bond to the tithe recorded here from its seat. Fresh.')
srow(106, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'BEN ZOMA: MIGHT THE TORAH SET A PARTITION BETWEEN THE FIRSTLING AND THE SECOND TITHE AS BETWEEN THE MOST HOLY AND THE LESSER HOLY? A REASONING: THE FIRSTLING NEEDS BRINGING TO THE PLACE, THE SECOND TITHE NEEDS BRINGING TO THE PLACE — AS THE FIRSTLING IS EATEN ONLY WITHIN THE WALL, SO THE SECOND TITHE. BUT THE FIRSTLING\'S PLACE IS NARROWED AS ITS TIME IS; THE SECOND TITHE\'S TIME IS WIDE — LET ITS PLACE BE WIDE! "AND YOU SHALL EAT BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD IN THE PLACE WHICH HE SHALL CHOOSE" — AS THE FIRSTLING, SO THE SECOND TITHE, ONLY WITHIN THE WALL. ({SP_(106, 3, "לפנים", "מן", "החומה")} "within the wall"; {SP_(106, 3, "הואיל", "ורבה", "זמן", "אכילתו")} "since its time of eating is wide"): I1 (checked) REFUTED, THEN THE VERSE — THE WALL OF JERUSALEM THE SECOND TITHE\'S BOUND, from the firstling (Mishnah Zevachim 5:8 the English\'s notes); the eating-place a parameter with the wall its value. Fresh.')
srow(106, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ISHMAEL: MIGHT A MAN BRING UP THE SECOND TITHE TO JERUSALEM IN THIS TIME AND EAT IT? A REASONING FROM THE FIRSTLING — EATEN ONLY WHILE THE HOUSE STANDS, SO THE SECOND TITHE; NO — THE FIRSTLING HAS BLOOD AND FAT FOR THE ALTAR; THE FIRST-FRUITS PROVE — NO BLOOD, NO FAT, EATEN ONLY WHILE THE HOUSE STANDS; NO — THE FIRST-FRUITS NEED SETTING DOWN BEFORE THE ALTAR. "AND YOU SHALL EAT BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD IN THE PLACE WHICH HE SHALL CHOOSE" — THE VERSE COMPARES THE FIRSTLING\'S EATING TO THE SECOND TITHE\'S: ONLY WHILE THE HOUSE STANDS. ({SP_(106, 4, "בזמן", "הזה")} "in this time"; {SP_(106, 4, "בכורים", "יוכיחו")} "the first-fruits prove"; {SP_(106, 4, "מקיש", "אכילת", "בכור", "למעשר", "שני")} "the verse compares the firstling\'s eating to the second tithe\'s"): I1 (checked) twice refuted, THEN THE JUXTAPOSITION ("the verse compares" — the shelf\'s own word, no code) — THE SECOND TITHE\'S EATING CONDITIONAL ON THE HOUSE: a STATUS tied to the place\'s standing (12b\'s design; the exam: Tosefta Sanhedrin 3:6, the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(106, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'OTHERS SAY: MIGHT A FIRSTLING WHOSE TIME PASSED FROM ONE YEAR TO ITS FELLOW BE DISQUALIFIED LIKE THE DISQUALIFIED CONSECRATED? "AND YOU SHALL EAT BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD." IF TO TEACH THAT THE FIRSTLING IS EATEN WITHIN THE WALL — NO NEED, "BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD YOU SHALL EAT IT" (15:20); IF OF THE SECOND TITHE — NO NEED, "YOU MAY NOT EAT WITHIN YOUR GATES" (12:17). WHY THEN? THE VERSE COMPARES THE FIRSTLING TO THE SECOND TITHE: AS THE SECOND TITHE IS EATEN FROM ONE YEAR TO ITS FELLOW, SO THE FIRSTLING. ({SP_(106, 5, "אם", "כן", "למה", "נאמר")} "if so, why is it said"; {SP_(106, 5, "משנה", "לחברתה")} "from one year to its fellow"): THE REDUNDANCY ARGUMENT — both seats already spoken (12:17 read at chapter 12; 15:20 NEVER READ AHEAD), so the clause teaches the juxtaposition\'s third law: the firstling past its year still fit. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 12\'s sitting).')
srow(106, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT YOU MAY LEARN TO FEAR THE LORD YOUR GOD" — IT TELLS THAT THE TITHE BRINGS A MAN TO THE STUDY OF TORAH. "ALL THE DAYS" — IN THE LAND AND OUTSIDE THE LAND. ({SP_(106, 6, "שהמעשר", "מביא", "את", "האדם", "לידי", "תלמוד", "תורה")} "that the tithe brings a man to the study of Torah"; {SP_(106, 6, "בין", "בארץ", "בין", "בחוצה", "לארץ")} "in the Land and outside the Land"): THE PURPOSE CLAUSE READ AS THE TITHE\'S EFFECT — the eating at the place a school (Tosafot\'s reading the exam\'s); "all the days" a status without a border; THE INK: "learn to fear" 4:10\'s and 17:19\'s kin (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(107, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WHEN THE WAY IS TOO LONG FOR YOU" (14:24) — MIGHT SCRIPTURE SPEAK OF A DISTANCE OF TIME? "THE PLACE IS TOO FAR FROM YOU" — OF A DISTANCE OF PLACE, NOT OF TIME. The head row of piska 107 ({SP_(107, 1, "ברחוק", "מקום", "הכתוב", "מדבר", "ולא", "ברחוק", "זמן")} "of a distance of place Scripture speaks, not of time"): THE CONDITION\'S MEASURE SPACE, NOT TIME — the two clauses read as one condition; THE INK: "the place too far" 12:21\'s clause verbatim (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(107, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY WHEN IT IS MUCH; WHENCE EVEN A LITTLE? "FOR YOU ARE NOT ABLE TO CARRY IT." ({SP_(107, 2, "מנין", "אפלו", "למועט")} "whence even a little"): THE THRESHOLD ZERO — any distance that bars the carrying releases the money (the exam: Mishnah Maaser Sheni 1:1?); the distance a parameter with the carrying its test. Fresh.')
srow(107, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY THE POOR; THE RICH WHENCE? "FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL BLESS YOU." ({SP_(107, 3, "אין", "לי", "אלא", "עני", "עשיר", "מנין")} "I have only the poor; the rich whence"): THE BLESSING CLAUSE READ AS THE RICH MAN\'S LICENSE — 14:24\'s fourth "for" a case, not a reason. Fresh.')
srow(107, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"THEN YOU SHALL TURN IT INTO MONEY" (14:25) — IT TEACHES THAT IT IS REDEEMED ONLY ON MONEY. WHENCE TO MAKE OTHER COIN LIKE SILVER? A REASONING FROM CONSECRATED PROPERTY — REDEEMED, AND OTHER COIN LIKE SILVER; BUT CONSECRATED PROPERTY TAKES OTHER MOVABLES TOO. "AND BIND UP THE MONEY" — A THING WHOSE WAY IS TO BE BOUND, R. ISHMAEL\'S WORDS; R. AKIVA: A THING THAT HAS A FIGURE ON IT — TO EXCLUDE A BLANK WITHOUT A FIGURE. ({SP_(107, 4, "שאין", "מתחלל", "אלא", "על", "הכסף")} "that it is redeemed only on money"; {SP_(107, 4, "דבר", "שדרכו", "לצרר")} "a thing whose way is to be bound"; {SP_(107, 4, "דבר", "שיש", "עליו", "צורה")} "a thing that has a figure on it"): I1 (checked) refuted, then "BIND" READ TWO WAYS — R. Ishmael\'s bundle, R. Akiva\'s stamp: THE MONEY\'S FORM A PARAMETER WITH TWO ARMS (Mishnah Eduyot 3:2 the English\'s note); THE INK: "bind up the money in your hand" ONE seat (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(107, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"IN YOUR HAND" — TO EXCLUDE WHAT WENT OUT OF YOUR DOMAIN. ({SP_(107, 5, "פרט", "לשיצא", "חוץ", "מרשותך")} "to exclude what went out of your domain"): the possession clause (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 1:2 the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(107, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND GO TO THE PLACE WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD SHALL CHOOSE" — THIS IS SHILOH AND THE ETERNAL HOUSE. ({SP_(107, 6, "זו", "שילה", "ובית", "עולמים")} "this is Shiloh and the eternal House"): THE PLACE FORMULA VALUED AT TWO STATIONS — chapter 12\'s eras table by CALL (the stations read from their cells); the formula\'s fifth seat (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(107, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL BESTOW THE MONEY ON WHATEVER YOUR SOUL DESIRES" (14:26) — R. JUDAH: MIGHT WHAT WAS BOUGHT WITH TITHE MONEY AND BECAME UNCLEAN NEED REDEMPTION? A REASONING FROM THE TITHE ITSELF — REDEEMED WHEN UNCLEAN. "MONEY" — THE FIRST MONEY, NOT THE SECOND MONEY. I HAVE ONLY THE CLEAN; THE UNCLEAN WHENCE? "MONEY" — THE FIRST MONEY, NOT THE SECOND. THREE "MONEYS" ARE SAID IN THE MATTER: ONE FOR CLEAN TITHE, ONE FOR UNCLEAN TITHE, ONE FOR WHAT IS BOUGHT WITH TITHE MONEY. ({SP_(107, 7, "כסף", "ראשון", "ולא", "כסף", "שני")} "the first money, not the second money"; {SP_(107, 7, "שלשה", "כספים", "נאמרו", "בענין")} "three moneys are said in the matter"): I1 (checked) OVERRIDDEN BY THE COUNT OF THE WORD — THE THREE "MONEY" TOKENS OF 14:25-26 (asserted: 14:25 two, 14:26 one) each a case: THE INK\'S COUNT THE LAW\'S TABLE (the English\'s note on the reduced text stands as the export\'s; Mishnah Maaser Sheni 3:10). Fresh.')
srow(107, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON WHATEVER YOUR SOUL DESIRES" — MIGHT IT BE ON SLAVES, MAIDSERVANTS AND LAND? "ON OXEN AND ON SHEEP." ({SP_(107, 8, "בעבדים", "ושפחות", "וקרקעות")} "on slaves, maidservants and land"): THE OPEN CLAUSE CLOSED BY ITS LIST — the four named the class (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 1:7 the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(107, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'I HAVE ONLY EATING; DRINKING WHENCE? "AND ON WINE AND ON STRONG DRINK." ({SP_(107, 9, "שתיה", "מנין")} "drinking whence"): the two liquids the drink\'s seat. Fresh.')
srow(107, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY EATING AND DRINKING; WHENCE EVEN WHAT IMPROVES EATING AND DRINKING — COSTUS, AMOMUM, HEADS OF SPICES, CROWFOOT, ASAFOETIDA, PEPPERS AND SAFFRON CAKES? "AND ON WHATEVER YOUR SOUL ASKS OF YOU." ({SP_(107, 10, "משביחי", "אכילה", "ושתיה")} "what improves eating and drinking"; {SP_(107, 10, "והפלפלים")} "and the peppers"): THE SECOND OPEN CLAUSE (14:26\'s "whatever your soul asks" — ONE seat, asserted) READ AS THE CONDIMENTS — the spice list the exam\'s row (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 2:1). Fresh.')
srow(107, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE EVEN WATER AND SALT? "ON OXEN AND ON SHEEP AND ON WINE AND ON STRONG DRINK" — AS THESE ARE DISTINCTIVE, FRUIT FROM FRUIT AND GROWING FROM THE EARTH, SO I HAVE ONLY A THING THAT IS FRUIT FROM FRUIT AND GROWS FROM THE EARTH. ({SP_(107, 11, "אף", "מים", "ומלח")} "even water and salt"; {SP_(107, 11, "פרי", "מן", "הפרי", "וגדולם", "מן", "הארץ")} "fruit from fruit and growing from the earth"): I3 (checked) — THE FOUR NAMED THE FATHER OF THE CLASS: two signs (fruit of fruit, of the earth) extracted from the list, water and salt out (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 1:5 the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(107, 12, 'CONTEXT', f'BEN BAG BAG SAYS: "ON OXEN" — YOU MAY BUY A COW BY WAY OF ITS HIDE. ({SP_(107, 12, "ולקחת", "פרה", "על", "ידי", "עורה")} "you may buy a cow by way of its hide"): the animal with its hide. Fresh.')
srow(107, 13, 'CONTEXT', f'"ON SHEEP" — YOU MAY BUY A EWE BY WAY OF ITS FLEECE. ({SP_(107, 13, "רחל", "על", "ידי", "גזתה")} "a ewe by way of its fleece"). Fresh.')
srow(107, 14, 'CONTEXT', f'"ON WINE" — YOU MAY BUY A JAR BY WAY OF ITS FLASK. ({SP_(107, 14, "חבית", "על", "ידי", "קנקנה")} "a jar by way of its flask"): the container with the wine (Mishnah Maaser Sheni 1:3 the English\'s note). Fresh.')
srow(107, 15, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND ON STRONG DRINK" — YOU MAY BUY GRAPE-SKIN WINE ONCE IT HAS FERMENTED. ({SP_(107, 15, "תמד", "משתחמיץ")} "grape-skin wine once it has fermented"): the strong drink read as the fermented (the English\'s note: Mishnah Chullin 1:7). Fresh.')
srow(107, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT ONE BUY A BEAST FOR HIS SON\'S FEAST? REASON: "REJOICING" IS SAID HERE AND "REJOICING" IS SAID THERE (27:7) — AS THERE PEACE OFFERINGS, SO HERE; OR AS THERE BURNT OFFERINGS AND PEACE OFFERINGS, SO HERE? "AND YOU SHALL EAT AND REJOICE" — A REJOICING WITH EATING; BURNT OFFERINGS, WHICH HAVE NO EATING, ARE OUT. ({SP_(107, 16, "נאמר", "כאן", "שמחה", "ונאמר", "להלן")} "rejoicing is said here and said there"; {SP_(107, 16, "שמחה", "שיש", "עמה", "אכילה")} "a rejoicing with eating"): I2 (checked) ON "REJOICE" WITH 27:7 (NEVER READ AHEAD — recorded from its seat), then the verse\'s own pair "eat and rejoice" the limit — THE REJOICING\'S FORM A PEACE OFFERING (the eating of the tithe\'s beast the peace offering\'s form; the English\'s notes); THE INK: "rejoice, you and your household" ONE seat, the book\'s eight rejoicings (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(108, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE LEVITE WITHIN YOUR GATES" (14:27) — WHEREVER YOU FIND THIS LEVITE, SAY: GIVE HIM OF HIS PORTION; IF HE HAS NO PORTION, GIVE HIM THE POOR MAN\'S TITHE; IF NOT, GIVE HIM PEACE OFFERINGS; IF NOT, SUPPORT HIM FROM CHARITY. The head row of piska 108 ({SP_(108, 1, "תן", "לו", "מחלקו")} "give him of his portion"; {SP_(108, 1, "פרנסהו", "מן", "הצדקה")} "support him from charity"): A LADDER OF FOUR FOR THE LEVITE — the first tithe (Numbers 18 by CALL), the poor man\'s tithe (14:28-29), the peace offering\'s meat, the alms: THE LEVITE\'S SUPPORT A STATUS WITH FOUR SOURCES IN ORDER; the English\'s note names the Levite\'s five seats (12:12, 12:18, 14:27, 14:29 — asserted; 26:11 ahead). Fresh.')
srow(108, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"FOR HE HAS NO PORTION NOR INHERITANCE WITH YOU" — TO TELL WHAT CAUSED IT. ({SP_(108, 2, "להגיד", "מה", "גרם")} "to tell what caused it"): the reason clause the cause; THE INK: the Levite\'s five seats of "portion and inheritance" (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(109, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AT THE END OF THREE YEARS" (14:28) — MIGHT IT BE AT THE FESTIVAL? "WHEN YOU HAVE FINISHED TITHING" (26:12). OR "WHEN YOU HAVE FINISHED TITHING" — The head row of piska 109 ({SP_(109, 1, "יכול", "בחג")} "might it be at the Festival"): THE END OF THE THIRD YEAR SOUGHT AS A DATE — the removal\'s day the question (26:12 NEVER READ AHEAD, cited from its seat; the English\'s note on the Festival of Huts). Fresh.')
srow(109, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE AT HANUKKAH? "END" — "END" IS SAID HERE AND "END" IS SAID THERE (31:10): AS THERE A PILGRIMAGE FESTIVAL, SO HERE A PILGRIMAGE FESTIVAL. ({SP_(109, 2, "יכול", "בחנכה")} "might it be at Hanukkah"; {SP_(109, 2, "נאמר", "כאן", "קץ", "ונאמר", "להלן")} "end is said here and end is said there"): I2 (checked) ON "END" WITH 31:10\'s SEVEN YEARS (asserted: "at the end of" the book\'s seven seats, 15:1 and 31:10 the kin; NEVER READ AHEAD) — a festival, not a winter feast. Fresh.')
srow(109, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'OR AS THERE THE FESTIVAL OF BOOTHS, SO HERE? "WHEN YOU HAVE FINISHED TITHING" — THE FESTIVAL AT WHICH THE TITHES ARE FINISHED: SAY, PASSOVER. FROM HERE THEY SAID: ON THE EVE OF THE LAST FESTIVAL DAY OF PASSOVER OF THE FOURTH AND OF THE SEVENTH YEAR WAS THE REMOVAL — IN THE FOURTH BECAUSE OF THE POOR MAN\'S TITHE OF THE THIRD, IN THE SEVENTH BECAUSE OF THE POOR MAN\'S TITHE OF THE SIXTH. ({SP_(109, 3, "הוי", "אומר", "זה", "פסח")} "say, this is Passover"; {SP_(109, 3, "ערב", "יום", "טוב", "האחרון", "של", "פסח")} "the eve of the last festival day of Passover"): THE DATE COMPUTED FROM TWO VERSES — the analogy gives a festival, 26:12\'s "finished" picks the one after the harvest: THE REMOVAL\'S DAY A CLOCK DATUM (Passover\'s last day, years 4 and 7 of the cycle — Mishnah Maaser Sheni 5:6 the English\'s note; the exam\'s row; the Sabbatical cycle 15:1\'s, ahead). Fresh.')
srow(109, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT EVEN THE SEVENTH YEAR BE LIABLE TO THE TITHE? "THE YEAR OF THE TITHE" (26:12) — A YEAR LIABLE TO THE TITHE; THE SEVENTH, NOT LIABLE, IS OUT. ({SP_(109, 4, "יצתה", "שנה", "שביעית")} "the seventh year is out"): THE SABBATICAL YEAR EXEMPT — the cycle\'s seventh no tithe (Exodus 23:10-11 by CALL, read at its sitting; 15:1 ahead). Fresh.')
srow(109, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT TWO TITHES BE PRACTISED IN IT? "THE YEAR OF THE TITHE" — ONE TITHE IS PRACTISED IN IT, NOT TWO. ({SP_(109, 5, "מעשר", "אחד", "נוהג", "בה")} "one tithe is practised in it"): THE THIRD YEAR\'S TITHE REPLACES, NOT ADDS — the poor man\'s tithe in place of the second (THE TWO TITHES OF THE CYCLE the design\'s table: years 1, 2, 4, 5 the second tithe; 3 and 6 the poor man\'s; 7 none). Fresh.')
srow(109, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'I HAVE ONLY THE POOR MAN\'S TITHE, OF WHICH SCRIPTURE SPEAKS; WHENCE THE OTHER TITHES? "THE TITHE OF YOUR PRODUCE" — IT INCLUDED. ({SP_(109, 6, "מעשר", "תבואתך", "רבה")} "the tithe of your produce — it included"): the removal covers every tithe. Fresh.')
srow(109, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOU SHALL BRING OUT ALL THE TITHE OF YOUR PRODUCE IN THAT YEAR" — IT TEACHES THAT THEY BRING IT OUT FROM A PLACE OF UNCLEANNESS TO A PLACE OF CLEANNESS. ({SP_(109, 7, "ממקום", "טמאה", "למקום", "טהרה")} "from a place of uncleanness to a place of cleanness"): "bring out" read literally. Fresh.')
srow(109, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT EVEN THAT OF OTHER YEARS BE BROUGHT OUT FROM UNCLEANNESS TO CLEANNESS? "IN THAT YEAR" — THAT YEAR\'S YOU BRING OUT, NOT OTHER YEARS\'; THAT YEAR\'S YOU REMOVE, AND YOU DO NOT REMOVE THE VEGETABLE THAT CAME OUT FROM THE NEW YEAR TO PASSOVER. ({SP_(109, 8, "של", "שנה", "ההיא", "אתה", "מוציא")} "that year\'s you bring out"; {SP_(109, 8, "מראש", "השנה", "ועד", "הפסח")} "from the New Year to Passover"): THE YEAR\'S EDGE FOR THE VEGETABLE — the tithe\'s new year and the removal\'s date joined (109:3\'s Passover; the exam: Rosh Hashanah 12a-b on the vegetables\' year). Fresh.')
srow(109, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND LAY IT UP WITHIN YOUR GATES" — IF THERE IS NO POOR MAN THERE, LAY IT UP IN THE STORE. ({SP_(109, 9, "הניחו", "באוצר")} "lay it up in the store"): the laying-up read as storage. Fresh.')
srow(109, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'I DO NOT KNOW WHICH IS SET ASIDE FOR THE POOR MAN\'S TITHE — THE FIRST TITHE OR THE SECOND? "AND THE LEVITE SHALL COME, FOR HE HAS NO PORTION NOR INHERITANCE" (14:29) — LET THE LEVITE COME AND TAKE HIS PORTION IN ANY CASE, R. JUDAH\'S WORDS. ({SP_(109, 10, "איני", "יודע", "מי", "ידחה")} "I do not know which is set aside"; {SP_(109, 10, "יבא", "הלוי", "ויטל", "חלקו", "מכל", "מקום")} "let the Levite come and take his portion in any case"): THE SECOND TITHE YIELDS, THE FIRST STANDS — the Levite\'s "no portion" clause the proof (109:5\'s one tithe decided: the poor man\'s replaces the second). Fresh.')
srow(109, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER SON OF JACOB: NO NEED — "AND TO THE SONS OF LEVI, BEHOLD, I HAVE GIVEN ALL THE TITHE IN ISRAEL FOR AN INHERITANCE" (NUMBERS 18:21): AS AN INHERITANCE DOES NOT MOVE, SO THE FIRST TITHE DOES NOT MOVE. ({SP_(109, 11, "מה", "נחלה", "אינה", "זזה")} "as an inheritance does not move"): THE LEVITES\' VERSE BY CALL (Numbers 18:21 read at its sitting) — the first tithe fixed by its name "inheritance" (the English\'s note: Sifrei Numbers 119). Fresh.')
srow(109, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT EVEN THE GLEANINGS, THE FORGOTTEN SHEAF AND THE CORNER BE LIABLE TO THE TITHE? "AND THE LEVITE SHALL COME, FOR HE HAS NO PORTION NOR INHERITANCE WITH YOU, AND THE SOJOURNER AND THE FATHERLESS" — THINGS IN WHICH HE HAS NO PORTION WITH YOU YOU GIVE HIM; THESE, IN WHICH HE HAS A PORTION WITH YOU, ARE OUT. ({SP_(109, 12, "אף", "לקט", "שכחה", "ופאה")} "even the gleanings, the forgotten sheaf and the corner"): THE POOR MAN\'S GIFTS EXEMPT FROM THE TITHE — the Levite shares them as a poor man (Leviticus 19:9-10, 23:22 by CALL; 24:19-21 NEVER READ AHEAD); the "no portion" clause the exemption\'s test. Fresh.')
srow(110, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE SOJOURNER AND THE FATHERLESS AND THE WIDOW WITHIN YOUR GATES" (14:29) — MIGHT IT BE WHETHER IN WANT OR NOT? DO NOT WONDER: "YOU SHALL NOT TAKE A WIDOW\'S GARMENT IN PLEDGE" (24:17) — POOR OR RICH! "THE POOR" (LEVITICUS 19:10) — AS THE POOR IS IN WANT, SO ALL OF THEM IN WANT. The head row of piska 110 ({SP_(110, 1, "בין", "חסרים", "ובין", "שאין", "חסרים")} "whether in want or not in want"; {SP_(110, 1, "מה", "עני", "חסר", "אף", "כלם", "חסרים")} "as the poor is in want so all of them in want"): I3 (checked) — THE FOUR\'S WANT THE CONDITION, from Leviticus 19:10\'s "poor" (by CALL) against 24:17\'s widow rich or poor (NEVER READ AHEAD — cited from its seat): the poor man\'s tithe to the needy alone. Fresh.')
srow(110, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE WHETHER SONS OF THE COVENANT OR NOT? "THE LEVITE" — AS THE LEVITE IS A SON OF THE COVENANT, SO ALL OF THEM SONS OF THE COVENANT. ({SP_(110, 2, "מה", "לוי", "בן", "ברית", "אף", "כלם", "בני", "ברית")} "as the Levite is a son of the covenant so all of them"): I3 (checked) — THE SOJOURNER OF 14:29 THE CONVERT (a son of the covenant), against 14:21\'s sojourner who eats the carcass (104:2\'s resident alien): THE ONE NOUN TWO PERSONS IN ONE CHAPTER — the exam\'s row (Yevamot 47b?). Fresh.')
srow(110, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED" — GIVE THEM ENOUGH TO SATISFY THEM. FROM HERE THEY SAID (TOSEFTA PEAH 4:2): THEY GIVE THE POOR AT THE THRESHING-FLOOR NOT LESS THAN HALF A KAV OF WHEAT OR A KAV OF BARLEY. ({SP_(110, 3, "תן", "להם", "כדי", "שבעם")} "give them enough to satisfy them"; {SP_(110, 3, "מחצי", "קב", "חטים")} "than half a kav of wheat"): THE MEASURE OF THE GIFT FROM "BE SATISFIED" — A QUANTITY, THE DATA CHANNEL (Mishnah Peah 8:5 the English\'s note; the Tosefta cited in the Hebrew); THE INK: "eat and be satisfied" ONE seat in this form (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(110, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITHIN YOUR GATES" — IT TEACHES THAT THEY DO NOT TAKE IT OUT FROM THE LAND TO OUTSIDE THE LAND. ({SP_(110, 4, "שאין", "מוציאים", "אותו", "מן", "הארץ", "לחוצה", "לארץ")} "that they do not take it out from the Land to outside the Land"): THE GATES THE LAND\'S — the poor man\'s tithe eaten in the Land (106:6\'s "all the days" in and out of the Land the contrast); THE INK: "within your gates" four seats in the chapter (asserted). Fresh.')
srow(110, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'THEY SAID: THE FAMILY OF THE HOUSE OF NEBALLATA WAS IN JERUSALEM, AND THEY GAVE THEM SIX HUNDRED TALENTS OF GOLD, AND THEY WOULD NOT TAKE THEM OUT OF JERUSALEM. The row without a citation ({SP_(110, 5, "משפחת", "בית", "נבלטה")} "the family of the house of Neballata"; {SP_(110, 5, "שש", "מאות", "ככרי", "זהב")} "six hundred talents of gold"): a run outside the Torah (the English\'s note: Tosefta Peah 4:11; 303:1-2 the parallel ahead). Fresh.')
